{
  "area": "stealth-actions",
  "description": "How a world’s authored rows become stealth actions, and what performing one does (US-2/US-3 of 121-stealth-and-perception). `actions` is the SHARED action block (`systems.actions`) and `columns` is stealth’s columns on those same rows (`WorldIR.perception.actions`) — never a second action table, the way CombatIR.actions extends the same rows. `expected.rows` is StealthActionTable.loadFromIR’s result in load order; `expected.facts` is what the table publishes back into the KB, which is `action/4`, `action_category/2`, `action_requires_target/1` and `action_target_type/2` and deliberately NOTHING stealth owns (§11 of docs/mechanic-predicates.md keeps per-act tuning out of the vocabulary — what a row PRODUCES is noise_level/2, concealed/1 and awareness/3, and those are already legible); `expected.effects` is what performing the row changes, as plain data the decision layer applies; and `expected.percepts` is the act as something there is to perceive, `null` for a row that authored no `presence` and is therefore imperceptible. The act’s percept id IS its enforcement event id, which is what makes witnessing the perception pass’s answer rather than a second ledger. Regenerate with `npm run stealth-corpus`.",
