    {
      "name": "stealth-columns-win-over-the-shared-row",
      "note": "The precedence, which is the thing four engines will each get subtly wrong: stealth column → shared row → unset, where a 0 on the shared row means unset (ActionIR defaults it to 0) and a value in a column was authored. Here the row authors a name and a cost and the columns override both, and everything that is stealth’s alone — presence, stance, concealment — has nowhere else it could have come from.",
